@rndquu does [this PR](https://github.com/ubiquity/devpool-directory/pull/1212) cover all aspects required for this larger task as well as the task in which it [links to](https://github.com/ubiquity/work.ubq.fi/issues/54)? - the issue timelines and PR threw me off at first, but below is correct yeah?
@CaptainPrinz after reading through this and related issues, I'm sure that you can work on refactoring the `work.ubq.fi` UI or the sync-solution immediately. The backend I think may be getting worked on at the moment by another contributor.
For the UI env vars, simply use the [exposed key and url](https://github.com/ubiquity/work.ubq.fi/blob/development/.github/workflows/cypress-testing.yml) to login and avoid rate limiting and then make the required changes using the existing issues.
For the sync solution, I believe this is workable but I'm not sure how you'd approach it. We want to ensure that the public and private repo can easily be kept in sync at the code level, not the issues.
Appreciate this. Some projects are moving to frameworks but most will likely stay as-is

The `Pricing: not set` is used purely to distinguish issues with and without price labels. The text itself is not used anywhere so it doesn't matter much whether it's `Pricing: -1`, `Pricing: not set`, etc...
@xno-miner Could you move the `Pricing: not set` string to a separate constant variable since it's used in multiple places ([one](https://github.com/xno-miner/devpool-directory/blob/8cdeed44ab0a42a694aca9d7641593e8dec66131/helpers/github.ts#L138), [two](https://github.com/xno-miner/devpool-directory/blob/8cdeed44ab0a42a694aca9d7641593e8dec66131/helpers/github.ts#L209))?
Otherwise the PR works fine.

